# ── The database and its sidecars ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Vault's data lives in ./data/ so it sits beside the code and is trivial to
# copy, but it is NEVER committed: it is personal data.
#
# Every path here is anchored with a leading slash. Without one, `data/`
# matches a directory of that name at ANY depth -- which silently excluded
# site/data/, the generated corpus the public demo is built from.
/data/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# ── Attachments, backups, logs, scratch ──────────────────────────────────────
/files/
/backups/
/inbox/
/logs/

# ── Python ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/

# ── OS noise ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
